# Clean UI / UX Generation Standards

Reference Skill: .agents/skills/clean-ui/SKILL.md

## 1. Less is More. Restraint is Taste
- Every visual element must earn its place by serving a clear communicative purpose.
- Follow the 70/20/10 rule: 70% neutral base, 20% secondary neutral/structure, 10% high-contrast brand accent.
- Avoid homogenous color goo: do not make every element the same color tint.
- Let whitespace and layout do the separation rather than unnecessary background boxes or heavy borders.

## 2. No Rounded-Square Icon Containers
- Never wrap icons in decorative rounded-rectangle pastel containers.
- Use icons inline or rely on typography and layout.
- Use consistent, professional vector SVGs rather than mixed icon libraries or emojis.

## 3. Typography & Hierarchy
- Clean, legible typography with reak-keep and -0.02em to -0.035em tracking for headings.
- Avoid decorative serif overuse or generic font combinations.
